   - \( 10 = 10 \) (implying \( n = p_1^9 \))
   - \( 10 = 5 \times 2 \) (implying \( n = p_1^4 \times p_2^1 \))
   - \( 10 = 2 \times 5 \) (implying \( n = p_1^1 \times p_2^4 \))

2. **Calculate Possible Values of \( n \)**:
   - For \( n = p_1^9 \): The smallest prime is 2, so \( n = 2^9 = 512 \).
