The cosine function has periodic properties, and we can use the fact that \( \cos(x) = \cos(y) \) if \( x = y + 2k\pi \) or \( x = -y + 2k\pi \) for any integer \( k \).

To convert degrees to radians, we use the conversion factor \( \frac{\pi}{180} \). Thus, \( t^\circ = t \cdot \frac{180}{\pi} \).

