This result indicates that there is a relatively low probability (approximately 22.22%) that two randomly chosen lengths from the interval \( (0, 3) \) will satisfy the triangle inequality when combined with a fixed length of 1. This highlights the constraints imposed by the triangle inequality in geometric configurations.
